      <activity id="959f8c53-434b-56c5-b6d9-4c350d571188" activityNameId="536838c6-a2af-554c-98d3-725ddef1b288" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Window frame, wood, natural/varnished, U=1.2 W/m2K, wall opening, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Window frame, wood, natural/varnished, U=1.2 W/m2K, wall opening, at plant
The measures of the window are 1.75m (width) x 1.3m (height). The wall opening is 1.8 m2 (assumption width of frame 0.12m, 2/3 of frame are behind the wall opening). 1m2 (wall opening) of wooden window frame weighs 20.7kg. The bill of materials is based on data from 3 window producers.;
UUID: 18eebcaa-19b5-37fa-8efc-bf5c06859cba
Included are the materials used in a wooden window frame (with surface treatment). Production losses, work materials, packaging materials, energy demand and the transport of the materials are also included.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data survey at 4 window manufacturers in Switzerland. 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_18eebcaa-19b5-37fa-8efc-bf5c06859cba.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
